body:
`DatabaseLoader` is fully implemented but never wired up — `MetadataPlugin` doesn't bridge the kernel's driver service to `MetadataManager`, and `register()` blindly broadcasts writes to all loaders including `FilesystemLoader`, crashing in read-only environments.

### MetadataPlugin: bridge driver in `start()`

Discovers `driver.*` services from the kernel registry and calls `manager.setDatabaseDriver()` to attach `DatabaseLoader`. This is the deferred setup path already designed in `setDatabaseDriver()` but never connected. Driver bridging is deferred until **after** filesystem metadata loading completes, so that system metadata populated via `register()` during bootstrap stays in-memory only and is not persisted to the database on every cold boot.

```typescript
// plugin.ts — start()
// 1. Load filesystem metadata first (in-memory only)
for (const entry of sortedTypes) { ... }

// 2. Bridge driver AFTER filesystem loading
const services = ctx.getServices();
for (const [serviceName, service] of services) {
    if (serviceName.startsWith('driver.') && service) {
        this.manager.setDatabaseDriver(service);
        break;
    }
}
```

### MetadataManager: scope `register()`/`unregister()` to writable `datasource:` loaders

- **`register()`** — only persists to loaders with `protocol === 'datasource:'` **and** `capabilities.write === true`, skipping `file:` and `memory:` protocols and respecting read-only datasource loader contracts
- **`unregister()`** — same dual filter applied for consistency

```typescript
for (const loader of this.loaders.values()) {
    if (loader.save && loader.contract.protocol === 'datasource:' && loader.contract.capabilities.write) {
        await loader.save(type, name, data);
    }
}
```

### Documentation

- Updated README architecture diagram to say "DatabaseLoader (datasource-backed storage)" instead of "planned", consistent with the loader status table marking it as "Implemented".

### Tests

13 new tests covering protocol + write capability filtering for both `register()`/`unregister()`, driver bridging lifecycle (driver found, no driver, `getServices` error), and call-ordering verification that driver bridging happens after filesystem loading. All 175 tests pass.
